!.vscode/extensions.json

# Agents. Worktrees are created in here and live inside the repo, so without
# this every parallel session shows up as untracked clutter in every other one.
# Ignored wholesale rather than by name, because whatever a future tool drops
# beside them is local state too. The two exceptions are the things the repo
# shares on purpose rather than accumulates: the permission allowlist, and the
# skills that encode this repo's own review and workflow rules — a skill only
# one machine has is a convention the next agent will not follow.
.claude/*
!.claude/settings.json
!.claude/skills/
